<title>LITHUANIA: GOVERNMENT BOOSTS MINIMUM SALARY.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT BOOSTS MINIMUM SALARY.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government has decided to increase the minimum salary to 400 litas from 330 litas, the government's press office said.</p>
<p>In a statement released late on Wednesday, the government's press office also said the minimum hourly payment was raised to 2.36 litas.</p>
<p>The new minimum salaries will come into effect from May 1.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
